Subject: Use <target> instead of <tasks> in the fix-sjk-core antrun execution

Origin: DHI-internal (same change as upstream stargate commit 8feb2f1b784ad72751ffe12047c61adde3a9f1ba, which only landed on the v1 branch)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/stargate/stargate.git 7e81d606bc44c39d211fd39c3c92444e3f8da349 path=coordinator
Regenerate: `sed -i 's#<tasks>#<target>#; s#</tasks>#</target>#' persistence-cassandra-4.0/pom.xml`
Verify: cmd `mvn clean install -Dmaven.test.skip=true -Dxml-format.skip=true -pl '!persistence-cassandra-3.11,!testing,!testing-services,!grpc-examples'` expect "BUILD SUCCESS"
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream's v1 branch already carries this change)
Drop-When: never: no stargate v2.0 release carries the change yet; drop this patch once the v2.0 pom itself uses <target>

The fix-sjk-core execution of maven-antrun-plugin in persistence-cassandra-4.0 configures its Ant tasks with the <tasks> element, which maven-antrun-plugin 3.0.0 and later no longer accept. The poms pin no antrun version, so the build fails once Maven resolves antrun 3.x. Using <target> keeps the same delete and jar tasks. The hunk matches the upstream v1 change except that it sits one line further down in the v2.0 pom.

--- a/persistence-cassandra-4.0/pom.xml
+++ b/persistence-cassandra-4.0/pom.xml
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@
               <goal>run</goal>
             </goals>
             <configuration>
-              <tasks>
+              <target>
                 <!-- Remove root package classes -->
                 <delete>
                   <fileset dir="${project.build.directory}/sjk-core/" includes="*.class"/>
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@
                   <fileset dir="${project.build.directory}/sjk-core"/>
                 </jar>
                 <delete dir="${project.build.directory}/sjk-core"/>
-              </tasks>
+              </target>
             </configuration>
           </execution>
         </executions>
